IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei1-benefit-period`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part I, "Special Benefits": ss 23.1 (compassionate care), 23.2 (critically ill
-- child) and 23.3(1) to (5) (critically ill adult; subsections (6) onward are piece ei2's). Layer 1 of piece ei1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
-- A week is identified by the DATE of its Sunday (the core). "Family member", "critically ill child" and "critically ill
-- adult" are the Regulations' (reg 1(3), (6), (7), piece er1) and are inputs; the prescribed class of medical practitioners
-- is reg 41.2 and the prescribed rules for dividing weeks are reg 41.6 (piece er3). No regulation in the deposited text
-- prescribes the shorter period of s 23.1(5), the "other circumstances" of ss 23.1(6)(c), 23.2(5)(c) and 23.3(4)(c), or
-- the "prescribed requirements" of the deferrals: each is an input.

§ `Section 23.1 - compassionate care benefits`

-- s 23.1(1): [Repealed, 2017, c. 20, s. 236] (src line 564). Nothing to encode.

-- src:566 | (2) Despite section 18, but subject to this section, benefits are payable to a major attachment claimant if a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued a certificate stating that
-- src:567 | (a) a family member of the claimant has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within 26 weeks
-- src:568 | (i) from the day the certificate is issued,
-- src:569 | (ii) in the case of a claim that is made before the day on which the certificate is issued, from the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies the family member’s medical condition, or
-- src:570 | (iii) in the case of a claim that is regarded to have been made on an earlier day under subsection 10(4) or (5), from that earlier day; and
-- src:571 | (b) the family member requires the care or support of one or more other family members.
-- src:587 | (5) If a shorter period is prescribed for the purposes of this section,
-- src:588 | (a) the certificate referred to in subsection (2) must state that the family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within that period; and
-- src:589 | (b) that period applies for the purposes of subparagraph (4)(b)(iii).
-- src:590 | Exception
-- The certificate must state that the family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within
-- 26 weeks (or the shorter prescribed period, subsection (5)(a)), counted from the day the certificate is issued, or the day
-- from which the practitioner certifies the condition if the claim was made first, or the earlier day under s 10(4) or (5).
-- The input is the number of weeks the certificate says, counted from that day.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(2), s 23.1(5)(a) (src:566-571) (src:588)
GIVEN `the number of weeks within which the certificate states that there is a significant risk of death` IS A NUMBER
      `the length in weeks of the shorter period prescribed for the purposes of section 23.1, if one is prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.1(2)(a) the certificate states that a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within the period` IF
    `the number of weeks within which the certificate states that there is a significant risk of death` AT MOST fromMaybe 26 `the length in weeks of the shorter period prescribed for the purposes of section 23.1, if one is prescribed`

-- src:573 | (3) In the circumstances set out in the regulations, the certificate required under subsection (2) may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners.
-- A member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners may issue the certificate in the circumstances set out in the
-- regulations (reg 41.2, piece er3).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(3) (src:573)
GIVEN `the practitioner is a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances set out in the regulations exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.1(3) the certificate may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` IF
        `the practitioner is a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners`
    AND `the circumstances set out in the regulations exist`

-- src:566 | (2) Despite section 18, but subject to this section, benefits are payable to a major attachment claimant if a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued a certificate stating that
-- src:567 | (a) a family member of the claimant has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within 26 weeks
-- src:568 | (i) from the day the certificate is issued,
-- src:569 | (ii) in the case of a claim that is made before the day on which the certificate is issued, from the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies the family member’s medical condition, or
-- src:570 | (iii) in the case of a claim that is regarded to have been made on an earlier day under subsection 10(4) or (5), from that earlier day; and
-- src:571 | (b) the family member requires the care or support of one or more other family members.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(2) (src:566-571)
GIVEN `the claimant is a major attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the family member requires the care or support of one or more other family members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.1(2) benefits are payable to the claimant for the care or support of a family member` IF
        `the claimant is a major attachment claimant`
    AND (`a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued a certificate` OR `the certificate may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners under subsection (3)`)
    AND `the certificate states that a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within the period`
    AND `the family member requires the care or support of one or more other family members`

-- src:591 | (6) Subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to a claim if
-- src:592 | (a) at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:593 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (4) has already been determined with respect to the family member, and the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:594 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(6) (src:591-594)
GIVEN `at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (4) has already been determined with respect to the family member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.1(6) subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` IF
        `at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted`
    OR (`the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (4) has already been determined with respect to the family member` AND `the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date`)
    OR `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`

-- The shape shared by ss 23.1(4), 23.2(3) and 23.3(3): the period begins with the first day of the week in which a given
-- day falls and ends on the last day of the week in which the first of the listed events occurs, the last of which is
-- the end of the 52 weeks (or a shorter period) following the first day of the first week. The 52 weeks following the
-- first day are the 364 days that begin with it, so they end on the Saturday before the first day 52 weeks on.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(4), s 23.2(3), s 23.3(3) (src:575-583) (src:615-622) (src:651-659)
GIVEN `a day in the week with which the period begins` IS A DATE
      `the days on which the events that end the period happen` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the length in weeks of the period after which it ends` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `ei1 the period that begins with the week of a day and ends with the week in which the first of the events happens` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the first day`, `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the first day` MEANS `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `a day in the week with which the period begins`
        `the end of the period of weeks following the first day` MEANS `the first day` PLUS (`weeks as days` `the length in weeks of the period after which it ends` MINUS 1)
        `the last day` MEANS
            `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing`
                (Date (minimum (map (GIVEN d YIELD Day d) (`the end of the period of weeks following the first day` FOLLOWED BY `the days on which the events that end the period happen`))))

-- src:575 | (4) Subject to section 12, benefits under this section are payable for each week of unemployment in the period
-- src:576 | (a) that begins with the first day of the week in which the following falls, namely,
-- src:577 | (i) the day of issuance of the first certificate in respect of the family member that meets the requirements of subsection (2) and is filed with the Commission,
-- src:578 | (ii) in the case of a claim that is made before the day on which the certificate is issued, the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies the family member’s medical condition, or
-- src:579 | (iii) in the case of a claim that is regarded to have been made on an earlier day under subsection 10(4) or (5), that earlier day; and
-- src:580 | (b) that ends on the last day of the week in which any of the following occurs, namely,
-- src:581 | (i) all benefits payable under this section in respect of the family member are exhausted,
-- src:582 | (ii) the family member dies, or
-- src:583 | (iii) the period of 52 weeks following the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (a) ends.
-- "Subject to section 12". The first day of the week in which falls (i) the day the first certificate that meets subsection (2)
-- is issued and filed, (ii) if the claim is made before the certificate is issued, the day from which the practitioner certifies
-- the condition (unless subsection (6) takes this out), or (iii) if the claim is regarded as made on an earlier day under
-- s 10(4) or (5), that earlier day. When more than one applies the Act does not say which; (iii), then (ii), then (i) is
-- the reading taken (fork F-23.1-4 in NOTES.md). The period ends with the last day of the week in which the first of
-- these happens: all benefits payable are exhausted, the family member dies, or the 52 weeks (or the shorter prescribed
-- period of subsection (5)(b)) end.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(4), s 23.1(5)(b) (src:575-583) (src:589)
GIVEN `the day on which the first certificate that meets the requirements of subsection (2) is issued and filed with the Commission` IS A DATE
      `the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies the family member's medical condition, if the claim is made before the day on which the certificate is issued` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the earlier day on which the claim is regarded to have been made under subsection 10(4) or (5), if it is` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which all benefits payable under section 23.1 in respect of the family member are exhausted, if they are` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the family member dies, if the family member has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the length in weeks of the shorter period prescribed for the purposes of section 23.1, if one is prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` IS
    `ei1 the period that begins with the week of a day and ends with the week in which the first of the events happens` `the day with which the period begins` `the days of the events` (fromMaybe 52 `the length in weeks of the shorter period prescribed for the purposes of section 23.1, if one is prescribed`)
    WHERE
        `the day with which the period begins` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the earlier day on which the claim is regarded to have been made under subsection 10(4) or (5), if it is`
            WHEN JUST earlier THEN earlier
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                CONSIDER `the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies the family member's medical condition, if the claim is made before the day on which the certificate is issued`
                WHEN JUST certified THEN IF `subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim under subsection (6)` THEN `the day on which the first certificate that meets the requirements of subsection (2) is issued and filed with the Commission` ELSE certified
                WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day on which the first certificate that meets the requirements of subsection (2) is issued and filed with the Commission`
        `the days of the events` MEANS
            append (`ei1 the dates in` `the day on which all benefits payable under section 23.1 in respect of the family member are exhausted, if they are`)
                   (`ei1 the dates in` `the day on which the family member dies, if the family member has died`)

-- src:585 | (4.1) For greater certainty, but subject to subsections (4) and 50(8.1), for benefits under this section to be payable after the end of the period of 26 weeks set out in paragraph (2)(a), it is not necessary for a medical doctor or nurse practitioner to issue an additional certificate under subsection (2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(4.1) (src:585)
GIVEN -- out of range: section 50(8.1) (piece ei2)
      `section 50(8.1) requires a further certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.1(4.1) an additional certificate is needed for benefits payable after the end of the period of 26 weeks` IF
    `section 50(8.1) requires a further certificate`

-- src:596 | (7) A claimant who makes a claim for benefits under this section may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period if
-- src:597 | (a) another claimant has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.06 in respect of the same family member during the period described in subsection (4) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period in respect of that claim;
-- src:598 | (b) another claimant is making a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.06 in respect of the same family member at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve the waiting period; or
-- src:599 | (c) the claimant, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.06 in respect of the same family member, meets the prescribed requirements.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(7) (src:596-599)
GIVEN `the claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 23.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another claimant has made a claim for benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 in respect of the same family member during the period described in subsection (4) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another claimant is making a claim for benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 in respect of the same family member at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 in respect of the same family member, meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.1(7) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` IF
        `the claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 23.1`
    AND (   `another claimant has made a claim for benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 in respect of the same family member during the period described in subsection (4) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period`
         OR `another claimant is making a claim for benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 in respect of the same family member at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve the waiting period`
         OR `the claimant, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 in respect of the same family member, meets the prescribed requirements`)

-- src:601 | (8) If a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.06 in respect of the same family member, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 152.06 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 26 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by those claimants.
-- src:602 | Maximum number of weeks that can be divided
-- src:603 | (8.1) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same family member, a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 152.06, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 152.06 that may be divided between them may not exceed 26 weeks.
-- The remaining weeks, up to 26, may be divided in the manner the claimants agree; (8.1) says for greater certainty that
-- the total divided between a claim under section 23.1 and one under section 152.06 may not exceed 26.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(8), s 23.1(8.1) (src:601) (src:603)
`s 23.1(8) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants` MEANS 26

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(8), s 23.1(8.1) (src:601) (src:603)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits divided to the first claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits divided to the second claimant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.1(8) the division of the remaining weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limit` IF
    `the weeks of benefits divided to the first claimant` PLUS `the weeks of benefits divided to the second claimant` AT MOST `s 23.1(8) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants`

-- src:605 | (9) If the claimants referred to in subsection (8) cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(9) (src:605)
GIVEN `the claimants agree on a division of the weeks of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.1(9) the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with the prescribed rules` IF
    NOT (`the claimants agree on a division of the weeks of benefits`)

-- src:607 | (10) When benefits are payable to a claimant for the reasons set out in this section and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons, the benefits payable to the claimant under this section shall be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.1(10) (src:607)
GIVEN `benefits are payable to the claimant for the reasons set out in section 23.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits payable to the claimant under section 23.1` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount by which the regulations reduce the benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23.1(10) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` IS
    IF `benefits are payable to the claimant for the reasons set out in section 23.1`
       AND `any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons`
    THEN max 0 (`the benefits payable to the claimant under section 23.1` MINUS `the amount by which the regulations reduce the benefits`)
    ELSE `the benefits payable to the claimant under section 23.1`

§ `Section 23.2 - benefits for a critically ill child`

-- src:609 | 23.2 (1) Despite section 18, but subject to this section, benefits are payable to a major attachment claimant who is a family member of a critically ill child in order to care for or support that child, if a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued a certificate that
-- src:610 | (a) states that the child is a critically ill child and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members; and
-- src:611 | (b) sets out the period during which the child requires that care or support.
-- src:612 | Medical practitioner
-- src:613 | (2) In the circumstances set out in the regulations, the certificate referred to in subsection (1) may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners.
-- src:614 | Weeks for which benefits may be paid
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.2(1), s 23.2(2) (src:609-611) (src:613)
GIVEN `the claimant is a major attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a family member of a critically ill child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are to care for or support that child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a medical doctor or nurse practitioner, or a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners in the circumstances set out in the regulations, has issued a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the child is a critically ill child and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets out the period during which the child requires that care or support` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.2(1) benefits are payable to the claimant to care for or support a critically ill child` IF
        `the claimant is a major attachment claimant`
    AND `the claimant is a family member of a critically ill child`
    AND `the benefits are to care for or support that child`
    AND `a medical doctor or nurse practitioner, or a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners in the circumstances set out in the regulations, has issued a certificate`
    AND `the certificate states that the child is a critically ill child and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members`
    AND `the certificate sets out the period during which the child requires that care or support`

-- src:615 | (3) Subject to section 12, benefits under this section are payable for each week of unemployment in the period
-- src:616 | (a) that begins on the first day of the week in which either of the following falls:
-- src:617 | (i) the day on which the first certificate is issued in respect of the child that meets the requirements of subsection (1) and is filed with the Commission, or
-- src:618 | (ii) in the case of a claim that is made before the day on which the certificate is issued, the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies that the child is critically ill; and
-- src:619 | (b) that ends on the last day of the week in which any of the following occurs:
-- src:620 | (i) all benefits payable under this section in respect of the child are exhausted,
-- src:621 | (ii) the child dies, or
-- src:622 | (iii) the expiry of 52 weeks following the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (a).
-- The first day of the week in which falls (i) the day the first certificate is issued and filed, or (ii) if the claim is made
-- before the certificate is issued, the day from which the practitioner certifies the child is critically ill (unless
-- subsection (5) takes this out); the period ends with the last day of the week in which all benefits payable in respect of the
-- child are exhausted, the child dies, or the 52 weeks following the first day of the first week end.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.2(3) (src:615-622)
GIVEN `the day on which the first certificate that meets the requirements of subsection (1) is issued and filed with the Commission` IS A DATE
      `the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies that the child is critically ill, if the claim is made before the day on which the certificate is issued` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which all benefits payable under section 23.2 in respect of the child are exhausted, if they are` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the child dies, if the child has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 23.2(3) the period during which benefits are payable` IS
    `ei1 the period that begins with the week of a day and ends with the week in which the first of the events happens` `the day with which the period begins` `the days of the events` 52
    WHERE
        `the day with which the period begins` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies that the child is critically ill, if the claim is made before the day on which the certificate is issued`
            WHEN JUST certified THEN IF `subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim under subsection (5)` THEN `the day on which the first certificate that meets the requirements of subsection (1) is issued and filed with the Commission` ELSE certified
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day on which the first certificate that meets the requirements of subsection (1) is issued and filed with the Commission`
        `the days of the events` MEANS
            append (`ei1 the dates in` `the day on which all benefits payable under section 23.2 in respect of the child are exhausted, if they are`)
                   (`ei1 the dates in` `the day on which the child dies, if the child has died`)

-- s 23.2(4): [Repealed, 2017, c. 20, s. 237] (src line 623). Nothing to encode.

-- src:625 | (5) Subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to a claim if
-- src:626 | (a) at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:627 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (3) has already been determined and the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:628 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.2(5) (src:625-628)
GIVEN `at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (3) has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.2(5) subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` IF
        `at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted`
    OR (`the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (3) has already been determined` AND `the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date`)
    OR `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`

-- src:630 | (6) A claimant who makes a claim for benefits under this section may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period if
-- src:631 | (a) another claimant has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.061 in respect of the same child during the period described in subsection (3) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period in respect of that claim;
-- src:632 | (b) another claimant is making a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.061 in respect of the same child at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve their waiting period; or
-- src:633 | (c) the claimant, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.061 in respect of the same child, meets the prescribed requirements.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.2(6) (src:630-633)
GIVEN `the claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 23.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another claimant has made a claim for benefits under section 23.2 or 152.061 in respect of the same child during the period described in subsection (3) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another claimant is making a claim for benefits under section 23.2 or 152.061 in respect of the same child at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under section 23.2 or 152.061 in respect of the same child, meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.2(6) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` IF
        `the claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 23.2`
    AND (   `another claimant has made a claim for benefits under section 23.2 or 152.061 in respect of the same child during the period described in subsection (3) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period`
         OR `another claimant is making a claim for benefits under section 23.2 or 152.061 in respect of the same child at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve their waiting period`
         OR `the claimant, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under section 23.2 or 152.061 in respect of the same child, meets the prescribed requirements`)

-- s 23.2(7): [Repealed, 2017, c. 20, s. 237] (src line 634). Nothing to encode.

-- src:636 | (8) If a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.061 in respect of the same child, any remaining weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 152.061 or under both those sections, up to a maximum of 35 weeks, may be divided in the manner agreed to by those claimants. If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- src:637 | Maximum divisible number of weeks
-- src:638 | (9) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same child, a claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and another claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 152.061, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 152.061 that may be divided between them must not exceed 35 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.2(8), s 23.2(9) (src:636) (src:638)
`s 23.2(8) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants` MEANS 35

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.2(8), s 23.2(9) (src:636) (src:638)
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits divided to the first claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits divided to the second claimant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.2(8) the division of the remaining weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limit` IF
    `the weeks of benefits divided to the first claimant` PLUS `the weeks of benefits divided to the second claimant` AT MOST `s 23.2(8) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants`

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.2(8) (src:636)
GIVEN `the claimants agree on a division of the weeks of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.2(8) the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with the prescribed rules` IF
    NOT (`the claimants agree on a division of the weeks of benefits`)

-- src:640 | (10) Benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable in respect of a child during the period referred to in subsection (3) or 152.061(3) that is established in respect of that child.
-- Compassionate care benefits are not payable in respect of a child during the critically-ill-child period for that child.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.2(10) (src:640)
GIVEN `the week falls in the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) that is established in respect of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.2(10) benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are payable in respect of the child for the week` IF
    NOT (`the week falls in the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) that is established in respect of the child`)

-- src:642 | (10.1) Benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 are not payable during the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (3)(a) in respect of a person who was a critically ill child if benefits were paid in respect of that person under this section.
-- The 52 weeks begin on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (3)(a).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.2(10.1) (src:642)
GIVEN `benefits were paid in respect of the person under section 23.2 when the person was a critically ill child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week falls in the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 23.2(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.2(10.1) benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 are payable in respect of the person for the week` IF
    NOT (`benefits were paid in respect of the person under section 23.2 when the person was a critically ill child` AND `the week falls in the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 23.2(3)(a)`)

-- src:644 | (11) When benefits are payable to a claimant for the reasons set out in this section and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons, the benefits payable to the claimant under this section shall be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.2(11) (src:644)
GIVEN `benefits are payable to the claimant for the reasons set out in section 23.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits payable to the claimant under section 23.2` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount by which the regulations reduce the benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23.2(11) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` IS
    IF `benefits are payable to the claimant for the reasons set out in section 23.2`
       AND `any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons`
    THEN max 0 (`the benefits payable to the claimant under section 23.2` MINUS `the amount by which the regulations reduce the benefits`)
    ELSE `the benefits payable to the claimant under section 23.2`

§ `Section 23.3(1) to (5) - benefits for a critically ill adult`

-- src:646 | 23.3 (1) Despite section 18, but subject to this section, benefits are payable to a major attachment claimant who is a family member of a critically ill adult, in order to care for or support that adult, if a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued a certificate that
-- src:647 | (a) states that the adult is a critically ill adult and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members; and
-- src:648 | (b) sets out the period during which the adult requires that care or support.
-- src:649 | Medical practitioner
-- src:650 | (2) In the circumstances set out in the regulations, the certificate referred to in subsection (1) may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.3(1), s 23.3(2) (src:646-648) (src:650)
GIVEN `the claimant is a major attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a family member of a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are to care for or support that adult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a medical doctor or nurse practitioner, or a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners in the circumstances set out in the regulations, has issued a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the adult is a critically ill adult and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets out the period during which the adult requires that care or support` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.3(1) benefits are payable to the claimant to care for or support a critically ill adult` IF
        `the claimant is a major attachment claimant`
    AND `the claimant is a family member of a critically ill adult`
    AND `the benefits are to care for or support that adult`
    AND `a medical doctor or nurse practitioner, or a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners in the circumstances set out in the regulations, has issued a certificate`
    AND `the certificate states that the adult is a critically ill adult and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members`
    AND `the certificate sets out the period during which the adult requires that care or support`

-- src:651 | Weeks for which benefits may be paid
-- src:652 | (3) Subject to section 12, benefits under this section are payable for each week of unemployment in the period
-- src:653 | (a) that begins on the first day of the week in which either of the following falls:
-- src:654 | (i) the day on which the first certificate is issued in respect of the adult that meets the requirements of subsection (1) and is filed with the Commission, or
-- src:655 | (ii) in the case of a claim that is made before the day on which the certificate is issued, the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies that the adult is critically ill; and
-- src:656 | (b) that ends on the last day of the week in which any of the following occurs:
-- src:657 | (i) all benefits payable under this section in respect of the adult are exhausted,
-- src:658 | (ii) the adult dies, or
-- src:659 | (iii) the expiry of the 52 weeks following the first day of the week referred to in paragraph (a).
-- The same shape as s 23.2(3), for an adult.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.3(3) (src:652-659)
GIVEN `the day on which the first certificate that meets the requirements of subsection (1) is issued and filed with the Commission` IS A DATE
      `the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies that the adult is critically ill, if the claim is made before the day on which the certificate is issued` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which all benefits payable under section 23.3 in respect of the adult are exhausted, if they are` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the adult dies, if the adult has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 23.3(3) the period during which benefits are payable` IS
    `ei1 the period that begins with the week of a day and ends with the week in which the first of the events happens` `the day with which the period begins` `the days of the events` 52
    WHERE
        `the day with which the period begins` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day from which the medical doctor or nurse practitioner certifies that the adult is critically ill, if the claim is made before the day on which the certificate is issued`
            WHEN JUST certified THEN IF `subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim under subsection (4)` THEN `the day on which the first certificate that meets the requirements of subsection (1) is issued and filed with the Commission` ELSE certified
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day on which the first certificate that meets the requirements of subsection (1) is issued and filed with the Commission`
        `the days of the events` MEANS
            append (`ei1 the dates in` `the day on which all benefits payable under section 23.3 in respect of the adult are exhausted, if they are`)
                   (`ei1 the dates in` `the day on which the adult dies, if the adult has died`)

-- src:661 | (4) Subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to a claim if
-- src:662 | (a) at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:663 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (3) has already been determined and the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:664 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.3(4) (src:661-664)
GIVEN `at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (3) has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.3(4) subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` IF
        `at the time the certificate is filed with the Commission, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted`
    OR (`the beginning of the period referred to in subsection (3) has already been determined` AND `the filing of the certificate with the Commission would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date`)
    OR `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`

-- src:666 | (5) A claimant who makes a claim for benefits under this section may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period if
-- src:667 | (a) another claimant has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.062 in respect of the same adult during the period described in subsection (3) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period in respect of that claim;
-- src:668 | (b) another claimant is making a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.062 in respect of the same adult at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve their waiting period; or
-- src:669 | (c) the claimant, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under this section or section 152.062 in respect of the same adult, meets the prescribed requirements.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23.3(5) (src:666-669)
GIVEN `the claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 23.3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another claimant has made a claim for benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 in respect of the same adult during the period described in subsection (3) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another claimant is making a claim for benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 in respect of the same adult at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 in respect of the same adult, meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23.3(5) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` IF
        `the claimant makes a claim for benefits under section 23.3`
    AND (   `another claimant has made a claim for benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 in respect of the same adult during the period described in subsection (3) and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period`
         OR `another claimant is making a claim for benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 in respect of the same adult at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve their waiting period`
         OR `the claimant, or another claimant who has made a claim for benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 in respect of the same adult, meets the prescribed requirements`)
